  "production_rules": [
    "A1 presentation is a visual overlay. It never changes walk, collision, stands, instance ids, cache ids, rewards, saves or A8 interaction state.",
    "All sprites are unscaled atlas frames on the 16 px grid. No per-site palette swaps and no non-integer scaling.",
    "Use OverworldOcclusion.configure_sprites for tall vegetation / architecture so the Hero remains readable.",
    "Lighting uses only A1-owned CanvasItemMaterials / Light2D nodes in isolated presentation; AVFX original Gold and A0 production lighting remain untouched.",
    "A0 alone mounts production scenes. A8 keeps local interaction art/engine; this grammar is a conformance target, not a takeover.",
    "Macro-terrain boundaries are authored causal landforms (geology/drainage/terrace/court/exposure), not random noise. Tile variant hash only selects texture inside an already-authored material.",
    "A1 world lights use a private CanvasItem cull mask; inherited Gold/Hero VFX remain on the default mask and are never ambient-tinted by A1.",
    "all 11 planned regions have a dedicated visual profile; 8 new regional windows are authored, not 192 chunk fills",
    "visual water only where source surface==water and walk==0; roads over water become explicit bridge/boardwalk overlays, never invisible walls",
    "Regional maintained crossings are narrow purposeful piers/causeways on authored spines; broad source road cells receive transparent wear decals, not opaque plank carpets.",
    "Impassable source water remains visually water/brine; only explicit source bridge/road cells may carry pier or causeway decks.",
    "Night readability uses A1-private lantern pools and raised ambient floors for hazard/destination silhouettes; original AVFX Gold remains untouched.",
    "Ecological detail clusters are authored landforms/decals, not random material confetti; frame totals are not a quality metric."
  ]
}
